    "rationale": "H-ABC is a TUBB4A-related leukodystrophy with a distinctive MRI pattern of hypomyelination, an absent or progressively disappearing putamen, and cerebellar atrophy. Dystonia, spasticity, and ataxia are common manifestations. Strongest alternative resolved: Vanishing white matter disease can produce progressive neurologic decline and diffuse white-matter abnormalities, but the combined hypomyelination, disappearing/atrophic putamen, cerebellar atrophy, dystonia and spasticity is the characteristic TUBB4A H-ABC pattern."
